    "description": "Jupiter Power LLC is a U.S. utility-scale battery-energy-storage platform that develops, owns and operates BESS projects serving energy, capacity and ancillary-services markets. Current company materials report 8,800 MWh operating, under construction or under contract and more than 20,000 MW in active development across eight U.S. RTO/ISO markets. BlackRock's legacy Diversified Infrastructure business announced the acquisition of Jupiter from EnCap Investments and co-investors Yorktown Partners and Mercuria Energy on November 15, 2022, and the acquisition closed on December 21, 2022. Jupiter now uses GIP-backed branding following BlackRock's October 2024 acquisition of GIP, but no separate Jupiter asset transfer or second GIP ownership period was disclosed. Austin, Houston and Chicago are disclosed office hubs; a single legal headquarters is not publicly disclosed. No later company sale or signed pending exit was identified through August 23, 2026.",
